Link wrote:
> Should wands of teleportation work 100% against the monsters on Astral
> (except Riders)?  It seems like it trivializes the end level of the
> game when I can literally teleport a big path around the Riders, and
> not have to deal with most of the scary monsters.

The wand of teleportation by itself isn't what makes Astral trivial.  If
that's all you're using, you'll have to meet at least one Rider,
possibly more.  I don't find much on Astral other than the Riders and
high priests scary.

Also, I usually find three or four per game.  I save them all, with all
the charges, except for occasional "you, horrible monster who is the
only immediate threat to my person, go away" zaps.  Because of this, I
can save my charging scrolls for wands of death.

The point of the previous paragraph?  Wands of teleport can be a highly
useful item from the very early game on.  If you AREN'T saving your
wands of teleport carefully and not using them constantly as get out of
jail free cards, then you'll end up needing other resources to take
advantage of them on Astral... either charging, markers to write
charging or something else.

I think of the benefits teleport wands give me on Astral as a reward for
playing the rest of the game in such a manner as to conserve resources
for when i'll _really_ want them.

